- micro service advantage and disadvantage
    Advantages of Microservices:
    	•	Enables independent development, deployment, and scaling of services.
    	•	Improves fault isolation—failure in one service doesn’t crash the whole system.
    	•	Allows use of different technologies for different services.
    	•	Enhances team productivity by letting teams work autonomously.

    Disadvantages of Microservices:
    	•	Complex to manage due to many moving parts and inter-service communication.
    	•	Difficult debugging and monitoring across distributed services.
    	•	Data consistency becomes harder to maintain.
    	•	Higher operational overhead with multiple deployments and CI/CD pipelines.
    In essence: Microservices offer flexibility and scalability but demand careful design, monitoring, and management to handle their complexity.

- why can't we scale RDBMS like NoSQL
    In brief:
        •	RDBMS follows ACID properties and joins, which make horizontal scaling (sharding) difficult.
        •	Data is tightly structured and relationships are enforced across tables, so distributing data across multiple servers breaks consistency.
        •	NoSQL, on the other hand, sacrifices some consistency for flexibility and partition tolerance, making it easier to scale horizontally by adding more nodes.

    In short: RDBMS is optimized for consistency and structure; NoSQL is optimized for scalability and flexibility.

